  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill with `name`/`description` front matter, so it is a site of `requirements.cli.skill_conventions.workflow`. The requirement says each skill must open, before any other section, with its workflow as ordered steps. This file meets that.\n\n- The only content before `## Workflow` is the `# Habeas requirements` title and a two-sentence intro. The intro is part of the title section and is not a separate section.\n- `section[Habeas requirements]/section[Workflow]` is the first subsection. It comes before `Writing chapters`, `Choosing references`, `What the review checks` and `Gotchas`.\n- The Workflow section is a numbered checklist of steps 1 to 7 (`- [ ] 1.` through `- [ ] 7.`), so the steps are ordered.\n\nThere are no violation queries to judge. The other bundled skills (`habeas`, `habeas-evidence`, `habeas-refactor`, `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`) use the same layout. I found no gap.",
